"""Append SOUND-2 report/metrics only after independently recorded PNG review."""
from pathlib import Path
import sys,json,hashlib
sys.dont_write_bytecode=True
from dsp2 import RECIPES,AMBIENCE_RECIPES
from verify2 import canonical,sha
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3];O=R/'Art/Audio';D=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
def run():
 b=json.loads((D/'baseline2.json').read_text());m=json.loads((O/'metrics-sound2.json').read_text());v=json.loads((O/'verification-sound2.json').read_text());review=json.loads((O/'visual-review-sound2.json').read_text())
 assert m['result']==v['result']=='PASS' and len(review['sheets'])==20 and v['files_verified']==20
 assert [{k:s[k] for k in ['file','sha256','size','audio_files']} for s in review['sheets']]==m['sheets']
 for s in review['sheets']:assert s['opened_individually'] and sha(O/s['file'])==s['sha256']
 aggregate=json.loads((O/'metrics.json').read_text());aggregate.pop('sound2',None)
 assert canonical(aggregate)==b['sound1_metrics_canonical_sha256'];aggregate['sound2']=m
 prefix=(O/'REPORT.md').read_bytes()[:b['sound1_report_prefix_bytes']]
 assert hashlib.sha256(prefix).hexdigest()==b['sound1_report_prefix_sha256']
 rows=m['files'];loops=[r for r in rows if r['channels']==2]
 lines=['','---','','## SOUND-2 — harbour dusk, Lighthouse Rock and new activity sounds','','Codex 2 (WSL CLI),2026-10-25. **Artist delivery complete by analysis:**18mono cues (6families ×3variants),2stereo30s loops. All20final per-file waveform/spectrogram sheets individually opened; no listening or Unity/native acceptance claimed. Claude owns copy/import, timbre, repetition and final mixer judgement.','','### Contract and integration','','All files are uncompressed RIFF WAVE,44,100Hz,signed16-bit little-endian PCM. Cue file names are `<Cue>_0.wav` through `_2.wav`; choose one per event. DogBark=.250s,Meow=.400s,Stitch=.200s,PotDrop=.800s; Puffin=.660/.720/.780s,Foghorn=2.900/3.000/3.100s. No downloaded audio, recordings, external samples, TTS or network generation: original deterministic numpy/scipy synthesis using unchanged SOUND-1 primitives. Pillow is for evidence images only. These are physically inspired approximations.','','Copy the18new cues to `Assets/Resources/Audio/SFX/` and the two beds to `Assets/Resources/Audio/Ambience/` when integrating; this task wrote no Assets or runtime files. Explicitly route new families and dusk/spot beds as appropriate. Treat Foghorn as a rare separate quiet cue; it is absent from LighthouseRock. Both loops are exactly1,323,000frames/channel: enable looping without extra silence, preserve sample counts and judge compression/import joins in the real player. One-shots have7ms tapers and zero first/last PCM samples.','','Dusk is2LU quieter than delivered HarbourDay (-30versus-28LUFS), with darker water/wind filters, two far gulls and exactly one church bell onset at20.1s (6.1s decay). No crickets. LighthouseRock has broader rock surf/open wind and five faint puffin calls; one surf wash wraps through the30s seam. Both retain live audio at the join. The8ms smooth endpoint bridge on each side gives identical endpoint values and zero slope steps; native perception of that short bridge remains part of ear acceptance.','','### Recipes','','| Family | Duration,s | Measured LUFS | Recipe |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for name,recipe in RECIPES.items():
  rr=[r for r in rows if r['family']==name];ds=[r['duration_seconds'] for r in rr];ls=[r['integrated_lufs'] for r in rr]
  lines.append(f'| {name} | {min(ds):.3f}–{max(ds):.3f} | {min(ls):.2f}–{max(ls):.2f} | {recipe} |')
 for r in loops:lines.append(f'| {r["family"]} | 30.000 stereo | {r["integrated_lufs"]:.2f} | {AMBIENCE_RECIPES[r["family"]]} |')
 lines+=['','### Actual decoded readings and individually opened sheets','','Each linked sheet belongs to its single delivered file. SFX rows show one waveform and absolute-level log-frequency spectrogram; loop sheets show both channels plus a±20ms seam zoom. Spectrogram range80Hz–16kHz,−100to−15dBFS; Foghorn’s~50Hz fundamental is below that plot range, independently confirmed in the decoded spectral check. Seam-row LUFS/peak is the full parent loop;40ms labels its zoom.','','| WAV | Opened sheet | Seconds | Sample peak,dBFS | Est.true peak,dBTP | LUFS | Zero pad,s |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in rows:
  stem=Path(r['file']).stem;lines.append(f'| [{stem}]({r["file"]}) | [wave + spectrum](review/SOUND2-{stem}.png) | {r["duration_seconds"]:.3f} | {r["sample_peak_dbfs"]:.2f} | {r["true_peak_4x_dbtp"]:.2f} | {r["integrated_lufs"]:.2f} | {r["measurement_zero_padding_seconds"]:.3f} |')
 lines+=['','[SOUND-2 metrics](metrics-sound2.json) records each file’s duration,format,frames,LUFS/padding,sample+4×estimated true peak,DC,RMS,endpoints,stereo correlation,seam value/slope and SHA256. The same data is added under `sound2` in [aggregate metrics](metrics.json); all original SOUND-1 keys/66rows retain their original semantic contents. [Synthesis inventory/event schedule](synthesis-sound2.json), [independent verification](verification-sound2.json), [actual individual review record](visual-review-sound2.json), [final receipt](delivery-receipt-sound2.json).','','LUFS uses the unchanged SOUND-1 BS.1770 K-weighting/gated400ms meter. DogBark and Stitch are zero-padded to400ms solely for measurement (150/200ms padding); these are padded energy readings. Known1kHz−20dBFSpeak test remains~−23mono/~−20stereo LUFS. Estimated true peak uses4×polyphase interpolation and is not a certified meter.','','Results:','',f'- Highest sample peak **{max(r["sample_peak_dbfs"] for r in rows):.3f}dBFS**; highest4×estimate **{max(r["true_peak_4x_dbtp"] for r in rows):.3f}dBTP**, below−3.',f'- Maximum cue-family loudness spread **{max(m["family_lufs_spread"].values()):.3f}LU**, below2; three unique PCM hashes per family.',f'- Maximum absolute DC **{max(abs(c) for r in rows for c in r["dc_offset_linear"]):.8f}FS**, below0.0007; all one-shot endpoints0 and adjacent samples within3PCMsteps.','- Independent exact86WAV inventory:66unchanged SOUND-1 +20SOUND-2.103original nonaggregate files retain exact size/SHA256. Original report’s15215-byte prefix unchanged. Both metadata exceptions are additive, as expressly requested by the brief.','','| Loop | Seam value,L/R | Seam slope,L/R | Join/whole RMS,L/R | Stereo correlation |','|---|---|---|---|---:|']
 for r in loops:
  s=r['loop_seam'];lines.append(f'| {r["family"]} | {s["value_step_linear"]} | {s["slope_step_linear"]} | '+', '.join(f'{x:.3f}' for x in s['join_to_whole_rms_ratio'])+f' | {r["stereo_correlation"]:.3f} |')
 lines+=['','Stitch cyclic variant overlap at8/12/16Hz over2s has worst unity-gain peak '+f'{max(r["unity_gain1_sum_peak_dbfs"] for r in m["stitch_overlap"].values()):.2f}dBFS; at0.65gain '+f'{max(r["gain065_sum_peak_dbfs"] for r in m["stitch_overlap"].values()):.2f}dBFS. This is a bounded stress case; still cap/review event rate and sum with music/water in the real mixer.','','### Reproduction and receipt scope','','New-only scripts: [dsp2.py](../Source/Audio/dsp2.py), [build2.py](../Source/Audio/build2.py), [analyze2.py](../Source/Audio/analyze2.py), [verify2.py](../Source/Audio/verify2.py), [run2.py](../Source/Audio/run2.py), [document2.py](../Source/Audio/document2.py), [finalize2.py](../Source/Audio/finalize2.py). [Protected original baseline](../Source/Audio/baseline2.json). Existing environment used; no installation.','','```sh','/home/mo/.venvs/catchline-ui/bin/python -B Art/Source/Audio/run2.py build analyze verify','```','','The historical SOUND-1 reproduction command above is superseded for this expanded directory: do not rerun its build/analyze/finalize scripts over the current pack; its exact66-file verifier is a historical inventory. New-only tooling reads unchanged old DSP/meter/plot primitives but writes only the20new WAVs and SOUND-2 evidence. If anything changes, open every affected final sheet again and explicitly replace its manual review record before document2.py/finalize2.py. The document script refuses stale review hashes.','','The original SOUND-1 receipt is preserved byte for byte. Its hashes for the two expanded aggregates (REPORT.md/metrics.json) are historical; the new SOUND-2 receipt supersedes those two only and binds new files, review hashes and the protected baseline proof. All other original receipt members remain unchanged. Artist completion is analytical; remaining lead acceptance is listening for believable vocal timbre, far bell/horn distance, repetition, loop-bridge perception and final gameplay/rapid-stitch balance. No git/commit,Unity,Assets,save or watchdog changes were made.']
 (O/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(aggregate,indent=2)+'\n')
 (O/'REPORT.md').write_bytes(prefix+('\n'.join(lines)+'\n').encode())
 print('SOUND2 DOCUMENT PASS20 file table rows; original prefix/metrics preserved',flush=True)
if __name__=='__main__':run()
